  <h2>The Components of Manufacturing Costs</h2>
  <p>Many factors influence the final unit price of your activewear. By understanding these, you can make better decisions for your brand's bottom line.</p>
  
  <h3>Cost Drivers</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Fabric Weight and Composition: Premium GSM counts cost more</li>
    <li>Construction Complexity: More seams and details increase labor time</li>
    <li>Order Quantity (MOQ): Larger orders benefit from economies of scale</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Optimization Tips</h3>
  <p>Standardizing fabric colors across multiple styles and choosing simpler logo placements can significantly reduce your per-unit costs.</p>
